---
import DocLink from '@/components/DocLink.astro';
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import ForFramework from '@/components/ForFramework.astro';
import HtmlExample from '@/components/motion/HtmlExample.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import { MotionRecipeNavReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-recipe-nav.tsx';
import { MotionRecipeNavAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-recipe-nav.ts';
import MotionRecipeNavSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-recipe-nav.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="recipes/navigation-menu"
  title="Motion: navigation menu recipe"
  description="A navigation menu whose submenus grow from their trigger while their links stay in the server HTML, in HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
  frameworkSwitch
>
  <h2 id="open-the-submenus">Open the submenus of a menu</h2>
  <p>
    Open a submenu of links from the menu bar: it grows from its trigger, and its links are in the page before it opens.
  </p>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">The button of each submenu has <code>aria-expanded</code>, and the list it opens has <code>hidden</code> and <code>data-motion="scale"</code>: setting <code>hidden</code> plays the exit, and removing it plays the entry.</p>
    <p slot="react">The demo is the Udixio <DocLink href="/components/menu/overview">Menu</DocLink> with <code>MenuSubmenu</code>: a closed submenu keeps its links in the DOM, hidden. Pass <code>lazy</code> to render a heavy one only while it is open.</p>
    <p slot="angular">The demo is the Udixio <DocLink href="/components/menu/overview">Menu</DocLink> with <code>udx-menu-submenu</code>: a closed submenu keeps its links in the DOM, hidden. Add <code>lazy</code> to render a heavy one only while it is open.</p>
    <p slot="svelte">The demo is the Udixio <DocLink href="/components/menu/overview">Menu</DocLink> with <code>MenuSubmenu</code>: a closed submenu keeps its links in the DOM, hidden. Pass <code>lazy</code> to render a heavy one only while it is open.</p>
  </ForFramework>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-recipe-nav" layout="split" previewHeight={288}>
    <HtmlExample slot="html" name="motion-recipe-nav" />
    <MotionRecipeNavReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionRecipeNavAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionRecipeNavSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2 id="why-it-is-accessible">Why it is accessible</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The menu sits in a <code>nav</code> with a name. Each submenu trigger exposes <code>aria-expanded</code>.</li>
    <li>
      <ForFramework as="span">
        <Fragment slot="html">In the HTML tab, Escape closes the open submenu, and with focus inside it, <code>data-motion-restore-focus</code> sends focus back to its button first.</Fragment>
        With the Udixio Menu, the arrow keys move between items, Arrow Right opens a submenu, and Arrow Left or Escape closes it and gives focus back to its trigger.
      </ForFramework>
    </li>
    <li>A closing submenu is <code>inert</code> at once, and <code>hidden</code> once its exit has played. Under reduced motion it opens and closes at once.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="motion-and-timing">Motion and timing</h2>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">The HTML tab plays the preset <code>scale</code> from its top-left corner (<code>origin-top-left</code>): <code>spring.default.spatial</code> and <code>spring.default.effects</code> in, <code>spring.default.effects</code> out.</p>
    <p>The Udixio submenu grows from the side of its trigger, from 80&nbsp;%, on <code>spring.fast.spatial</code>, and fades in on <code>spring.fast.effects</code>; it leaves faster, on <code>spring.fast.effects</code>.</p>
  </ForFramework>
</MotionPage>
